	<string>$(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER)</string>
	<!-- Sign in with Google. Two values, both from the iOS OAuth client in the Google
	     Cloud console (Application type: iOS, bundle id social.poppys.app):

	       GIDClientID        the Client ID          123-abc.apps.googleusercontent.com
	       CFBundleURLSchemes the iOS URL scheme     com.googleusercontent.apps.123-abc
	                          (the same id, dot-fields reversed)

	     There is no client secret for an iOS client: Google verifies the app by its
	     bundle id instead, which is why the bundle id here and there must match exactly.
	     Leave these placeholders and sign-in stays unavailable; the app falls back to
	     asking for a name and an email rather than failing. -->
